</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5da151c-d11b-11f1-a017-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090715-090917-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5da151c-d11b-11f1-a017-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090715-090917-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">faeea4e6-d11b-11f1-ab7e-0d72754faf20</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:55:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Serbia's student movement ousts longtime leader Vucic in parliament poll</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-student-movement-ousts-longtime-leader-vucic-in-parliament-poll</link><description>
Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat in an historic election on Sunday (October 25) following a near to 70% turnout at polling stations. The snap election followed nearly two years of student-led demonstrations against perceived corruption and authoritarianism triggered by the deaths of 16 people when a train station canopy collapsed in the ‌city of Novi Sad in 2024. FRANCE 24's Laurent Rouy tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/633333c2-d118-11f1-875e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-081316-081819-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/633333c2-d118-11f1-875e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-081316-081819-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68b45fa6-d118-11f1-bf67-678a93ac0221</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:41:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat in historic snap election with record turnout</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-historic-snap-election-with-record-turnout</link><description>
Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat in an historic election on Sunday following a near to 70% turnout at polling stations – the highest since the break-up of Yugoslavia in 1992. The snap election followed nearly two years of student-led demonstrations against perceived corruption and authoritarianism triggered by the deaths of 16 people when a train station canopy collapsed in the ‌city of Novi Sad in 2024.  
